---
const items = [
  {
    q: "Does Hondo answer every message?",
    a: "No. It answers mentions and direct messages. In a thread that it joined, it answers only the messages that are for it, and stays quiet when people talk among themselves.",
  },
  {
    q: "Can it change things in production?",
    a: "It can use only the tools that an admin approved, and only in the channels that an admin picked. Before a tool that can change data runs, Hondo posts the call in the thread, and a person in the channel must approve it. An admin can turn this off for each tool.",
  },
  {
    q: "How do I know an answer is correct?",
    a: "Each claim comes from a tool result. Ask for sources, and Hondo shows the tools, the queries and the links. When a lookup finds nothing, it tells you what it searched.",
  },
  {
    q: "Which tools can it use?",
    a: "GitHub and Atlassian are built in. You can also connect any remote MCP server with OAuth or a key, for example the official server of your logs or metrics tool. For an API without an MCP server, an admin can make each HTTP request into a tool.",
  },
  {
    q: "Which models does it use?",
    a: "The model that you choose, through Vercel AI Gateway, OpenAI or Anthropic. You bring the key.",
  },
  {
    q: "Where does our data go?",
    a: "Conversations and thread summaries stay in your Postgres. The model provider gets the context it needs to answer, and connected tools get the calls that Hondo makes.",
  },
  {
    q: "What if Hondo crashes in the middle of a run?",
    a: "The run continues from its recorded steps after a restart, and nothing posts twice. A failure stops that one run only.",
  },
  {
    q: "Is it free?",
    a: "Yes. Hondo is open source under the Apache-2.0 license. You run it on your servers and pay only your model provider.",
  },
];
---

<section class="section wrap" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <div class="faq">
    <h2 class="duo" id="faq-title">
      your questions <span>answered</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="list">
      {items.map((item) => (
        <details>
          <summary>
            {item.q}
            <span class="plus" aria-hidden="true" />
          </summary>
          <p>{item.a}</p>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .faq {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.5fr;
    gap: clamp(32px, 6vw, 80px);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .faq h2 {
    position: sticky;
    top: 112px;
  }

  details {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  details:first-child {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  details::details-content {
    block-size: 0;
    overflow: clip;
    transition:
      block-size 320ms var(--ease-drawer),
      content-visibility 320ms allow-discrete;
  }

  details[open]::details-content {
    block-size: auto;
  }

  @supports (interpolate-size: allow-keywords) {
    :root {
      interpolate-size: allow-keywords;
    }
  }

  summary {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 24px;
    padding: 20px 0;
    font-size: 17px;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    list-style: none;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .plus {
    position: relative;
    flex: none;
    width: 12px;
    height: 12px;
    color: var(--dust);
  }

  .plus::before,
  .plus::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: 5.25px 0;
    background: currentColor;
    transition: transform 260ms var(--ease-out);
  }

  .plus::after {
    transform: rotate(90deg);
  }

  details[open] .plus::after {
    transform: rotate(0deg);
  }

  p {
    max-width: 36em;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0 0 22px;
    color: var(--muted);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .faq {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .faq h2 {
      position: static;
    }
  }
</style>
